    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34771" root="فوج" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَائِجٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَوْجٌ</span>. One says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرَّ بِنَا فَائِجُ وَلِيمَةِ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُلَانٍ</span>, meaning <i>The company</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَوْج</span>) <i>of those that
were at the repast of such a one</i> [<i>passed by us</i>].
(TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  It is said that <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَائِجٌ</span>, applied to a she-camel, signifies <i>Fat:</i> or <i>such as is termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَائِل</span>,
<i>and fat:</i> but the word commonly known [thus
used] is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَائِجٌ</span> [q. v.]. (TA.)

  </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
